# StigReady site — brand & SEO

## Product naming

- **StigReady Base** — STIG disk layout + cloud hardening; bring your own profiles/roles
- **StigReady Applied** — CIS L1/L2 or DISA STIG remediated AMIs with published scores
- **StigForge** — public Ansible role exports (`stigready/*-cis`, `*-stig`) + scores on `/#stigforge`

## Hard no

- Never link or CTA to private monorepo `github.com/stigready/stigforge`
- Never put AMI IDs, snapshot IDs, account IDs, or evidence-bucket paths on the public site
- Do not reintroduce Marketplace **Coming soon** status columns — listing state is not tracked on the site
- Do not invent Applied cells (e.g. AL2023 CIS/STIG) that are not in AWS / `catalog.json`
- RHEL is **BYOL** — say so; we do not sell Red Hat licenses

## SEO when adding HTML

Every new public page needs: unique title + description, absolute canonical, OG/Twitter tags, favicon, GA `G-R2J9HMP1XX`, and a `sitemap.xml` entry. Blog posts use `BlogPosting` JSON-LD.

## Nav / footer

Match home: Base · Applied · StigForge · Blog · Pricing · Contact.

## Logos

- Site (navy bg): `assets/logo.png` / `logo.svg` (white STIG)
- Marketplace / light bg: `assets/logo-on-light.png` / `logo-on-light.svg`

## Content ops

- Public blog = published list only (`blog/index.html`)
- Upcoming posts queue = `docs/blog-roadmap.md` (maintainer only — do not render on the site)
- Skills: `blog-ship`, `seo-audit`, `marketplace-copy`, `ami-site-sync`
